   "name": "Chemical symbols",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A chemical symbol is a shorthand way of writing an element. A one-letter symbol is a capital, like O. A two-letter symbol has a capital then a small letter, like Ca. Some symbols come from Latin names: Na is sodium from Natrium, K is potassium from Kalium."
    }
   },
